<BaseLayout title="What's New" description="Latest updates on HCA certification timelines and exam options from Headway Nursing Services.">
  <div class="prose prose-slate mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12">
    <h1>What's New</h1>

    <h2>Extension of 200-day deadline to 365 days</h2>
    <p>
      Per Senate Bill 5672, the home care aide program has adopted emergency rules under WSR 25-18-034
      to allow home care aides to work for up to <strong>365 days</strong> from their date of hire. This
      timeline change is retroactive. Any home care aide applicant who is working while completing their
      training, testing, and credentialing process can now work for up to 365 days from their date of
      hire, regardless of whether they previously passed their 200-day timeline.
    </p>
    <p>
      If a home care aide has already passed 365 days and is still waiting to be credentialed, their
      employer may provide the Department of Health with an updated date of hire to start the timeline
      over with an additional 365 days. The requirement to complete training within 120 days of the date
      of hire has not changed.
    </p>
    <p>
      The 365-day extension timeline expires on <strong>December 31, 2027</strong>. Anyone who provides
      the Department of Health with an application after that date will be allowed only 200 days to work
      while they complete the credentialing process.
    </p>

    <h2>2025 — Online remote knowledge exam option</h2>
    <p>
      As of March 11, 2025, Prometric now offers an online option to take the knowledge exams through
      ProProctor. Before choosing this option, read the ProProctor User Guide. See the Candidate Portal
      to ensure your system meets the necessary operating and hardware requirements. Online testing is
      currently available only in English.
    </p>

    <h2>HCA exam application resources</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>File your application using the DOH online portal for timely processing.</li>
      <li>Self-schedule examinations through the Prometric portal.</li>
      <li>Knowledge exam: 60 questions. Clinical exam covers various timed skills.</li>
      <li>DOH Navigators are available to assist with the certification process.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Key contacts</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>DOH HCA Credentialing: (360) 236-2700</li>
      <li>DOH Customer Service: (360) 236-4700</li>
      <li>Prometric: 1-800-324-4689</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      <a href="/hca-exam">Full HCA exam steps →</a> ·
      <a href="https://www.dshs.wa.gov/altsa/home-and-community-services/training-requirements-and-classes" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">DSHS training requirements</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
